@* The × every dialog wears, in the two places a dialog puts it.

   Inline (the default) is a sibling of the title and the search box in a picker's header row, so
   it is input-height and washes with ink like the other controls beside it.

   Floating sits in the corner of a detail sheet's tinted header band, over a colour the sheet
   chooses — so it is a size smaller, to sit clear of the heading it overlaps, and washes with
   white, which is the one wash that reads the same over every tint.

   ModalShell already closes on Escape and on a backdrop click; this is the visible affordance. *@

<button type="button" @onclick="OnClick" aria-label="Close" class="@CssClass">
    <Icon Name="x" Class="w-5 h-5"/>
</button>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnClick { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Pins it to the top-right corner of a tinted header band. See the note above.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Floating { get; set; }

    private string CssClass =>
        "inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-500 hover:text-ink-900 transition-colors focus-ring "
        + (Floating
            ? "absolute top-4 right-4 h-8 w-8 hover:bg-white/60"
            : "h-9 w-9 shrink-0 hover:bg-ink-100");
}
